           power of 2 =>  (n & (n-1))==0  .   
          so if a number is power of 2 then that number will contain only one set bit WHILE others will comtain more than one set bit so for that 
          particular number that is power of 2 we are finding the position where the set is present.

CODE : 

class Solution {
public:
    int findPosition(int n) {
        // code here

        if ((n & (n - 1)) == 0)
        {
            int count = 1;

            while (n)
            {
                if (n & 1)
                    return count;

                count++;
                n = n >> 1;
            }
        }
        else
            return -1;
    }
};


